<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="022" project="messaging-communication-app-r3">
  <metadata>
    <title>Forward action on a message → email modal in forward mode, prefilled (FR-08)</title>
    <phase>3 Email-in-flow + quick-view + new-thread</phase>
    <gate>after:020</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Extends the shared send UI (forward mode) — ADR-045 blast radius; edits SendEmailDialog/EmailComposer. Code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Reuses the send engine's existing forward/reply mode machinery; prefill wiring is well-specified.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Extends SendEmailDialog from task 020 — same files; must serialize.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>020</deps>
    <tags>frontend, react</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>Add a Forward action to a message in the conversation flow that opens the email modal (`SendEmailDialog`) in FORWARD mode, prefilled with the source message's subject/body/attachments per the composer's existing forward semantics. Drafts live ONLY in the email modal — the conversation does not persist a draft. Reuse the composer's existing send-mode machinery (`SendModeRadio` / send modes) — do NOT invent a new forward flow or send path.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in React 18 + Fluent UI v9 + Spaarke shared component libs.</role>
  <goal>A Forward affordance on a message opens the extended SendEmailDialog in forward mode, prefilled from the source; the draft lives only in the modal; forward reuses the existing send path with the active thread/regarding context; keyboard + ARIA; dark-mode compliant.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-08 requires forwarding a message via the email modal in forward mode, prefilled. The EmailComposer already supports send modes (see `SendModeRadio.tsx` / `EmailComposer.reducer.ts`). Task 020 extended `SendEmailDialog` to accept thread id + regarding; forwarding reuses that. The conversation itself never stores a draft — the modal owns it.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/wrappers/SendEmailDialog.tsx</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/subcomponents/SendModeRadio.tsx</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/EmailComposer.reducer.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/ConversationView/ConversationView.tsx</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>020 (extended SendEmailDialog with thread/regarding) merged. The composer's existing forward/send-mode support.</dependencies>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-08">Forward opens the email modal in forward mode, prefilled from the source message; drafts live ONLY in the email modal (no conversation-side draft persistence).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">Reuse the existing composer send-mode machinery + send path; no new forward send implementation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 semantic tokens; light + dark via host FluentProvider.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-05">Forward affordance keyboard-operable + ARIA-labeled.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-045-communication-send-engine.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Send-mode radio" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/subcomponents/SendModeRadio.tsx">Existing forward/reply/new send-mode control — reuse for forward mode.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Confirm the composer's forward mode + prefill contract in `EmailComposer.reducer.ts` / `SendModeRadio.tsx` (what fields it prefills: subject `Fwd:`, quoted body, attachments).</step>
    <step order="2">Add a Forward action (menu item / icon) on messages in ConversationView; on activate, open `SendEmailDialog` in forward mode seeded from the source message + active thread/regarding.</step>
    <step order="3">Ensure prefill uses the composer's existing forward semantics; the conversation stores no draft (modal owns state).</step>
    <step order="4">Keyboard + ARIA on the Forward action.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests: Forward opens modal in forward mode prefilled from source; draft not persisted in conversation on cancel; send uses existing path with thread/regarding; dark mode.</step>
    <step order="6">Run component tests/build (`npm run build` for the non-PCF package + vitest).</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md 🔲 → ✅.</step>
    <step order="8">Document deviations in `projects/messaging-communication-app-r3/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the composer has no existing forward mode to reuse (requiring a net-new send flow), STOP and escalate — do not build a parallel forward send path (ADR-045).</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build TS/React + run vitest</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">shell</tool>
  </tools>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/ConversationView/ConversationView.tsx</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/ConversationView/__tests__/ConversationView.forward.test.tsx</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A Forward action on a message opens `SendEmailDialog` in FORWARD mode, prefilled (subject/body/attachments) via the composer's existing forward semantics.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The forward reuses the existing send path with the active thread + regarding context; no new forward send implementation.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cancelling the forward leaves NO draft persisted in the conversation (draft lives only in the modal).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Forward affordance keyboard-operable + ARIA-labeled (NFR-05).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Dark mode passes via host FluentProvider (ADR-021) — semantic tokens only.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Component tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Forward opens prefilled modal"><steps><step>Activate Forward on a message</step></steps><expected>SendEmailDialog opens in forward mode, prefilled from the source message.</expected></test>
    <test name="No conversation-side draft"><steps><step>Open forward, type, cancel</step></steps><expected>No draft persisted in the conversation.</expected></test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)"><steps><step>Toggle dark mode</step><step>Verify semantic tokens adapt</step></steps><expected>No hardcoded colors.</expected></test>
  </ui-tests>
  <notes>Reference spec FR-08. Reuse the composer's existing send-mode/forward machinery; the modal owns the draft.</notes>
  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill><protocol>Load knowledge files first; follow task-execute.</protocol></execution>
</task>
